\f0\fs36 \cf0 Read_Me for code and data associated with the manuscript, \'93Deriving Quantitative Signals from Replicated DNA Metabarcoding\'94\
\
\

\f1\b /NIMBLE Simulation -
\f0\b0  Contains scripts for generating simulations of metabarcoding data and estimating models for simulation output using Nimble (Model A as described in Supplement S1).  There are separate subfolders and scripts for analyzing data from a single marker (1_marker) and for combining data from two markers (2_marker)\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 /NIMBLE Simulation/1_marker/ Nimble_single_marker_sim.R -
\f0\b0  This is a script for simulating and estimating DNA concentrations from  metabarcoding data from a single metabarcoding marker. It can be modified to simulate an arbitrary number of species and metabarcoding replicates, following user specified observation dynamics.  The script calls the functions in the folder shared_functions. A NIMBLE model is defined and run within the script (Model A in Supplement S1).
\f1\b \
